target/
Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
*.capture.local
.superpowers/
# Agent worktrees + local harness state
.claude/*
# …except the project's own skills. Those are documentation of how this repo is
# worked on, they go stale when the code moves, and a cleanup pass re-verifies
# them against the binary — none of which works if they live only on one machine.
# The parent is `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a negation under one never matches.
!.claude/skills/
# …and the shared project settings, which carry the PostToolUse auto-rustfmt
# hook (see CLAUDE.md → Formatting). It has to ship so every clone formats on
# edit, not just this machine. Same `.claude/*`-not-`.claude/` rule as above:
# re-including a single file under an excluded-by-glob parent works.
!.claude/settings.json

# --- research working dir: exclude junk + third-party/proprietary content ---
# Regenerable tooling state
research/**/.venv/
research/**/__pycache__/
research/**/*.pyc
# Proprietary vendor binaries (Ross-Tech VCDS/loader/DLL) — not ours to redistribute
research/clb-crack/bin/
# Third-party reference source + proprietary label/rod DB inputs
research/clb-crack/ref/
research/clb-crack/samples/
# Decoded proprietary label content (RE outputs, not for redistribution)
research/clb-crack/decoded_*.txt
# USB captures: large + contain private vehicle data
research/captures/*.pcapng
research/dumps/
research/logs/

# VCDS install symlinks — proprietary Ross-Tech label/ODX data, never commit
research/vcds-data/

# Capture artifacts written by `vagcan sniff` / `scan-dids`: bus traffic from a
# real car, so they carry the VIN. Never committed.
/*.jsonl
research/dumps/
research/logs/
# The VCDS installations moved to vendor/, archived and LFS-tracked. Their own
# vendor/.gitignore keeps the unpacked copies local; only vendor/*.zip is in Git.

# Browser session artifacts from Playwright — logs and DOM snapshots, never source.
.playwright-mcp/

# Generated by `measure view` next to its input; the sample JSON is the source.
crates/vagcan/src/measure/view_sample.html

# Nothing this tool reads at run time lives in the checkout. Two kinds of file
# used to, and neither may be published:
#
#   names-uds.json, rod-iv-cache.json   derived from a Ross-Tech VCDS
#                                       installation, so not ours to
#                                       redistribute — `vagcan setup` recovers
#                                       them into ~/.vagcan/labels/
#   vehicles/*.json                     measurement rows proven on one owner's
#                                       car; another car needs its own, built by
#                                       `vagcan recording calibrate`
#
# They are still on disk for anyone who has them; git simply does not carry
# them. See crates/vagcan/src/datadir.rs for where the tool looks now.
catalogs/

# Unpacked VCDS installations sitting beside the archives. The archives
# themselves are LFS objects and are carried; an unpacked copy is 300 MB of the
# same bytes.
vendor/vcds-*/

.worktrees/
